cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these workflows, please cite the archived software release and the relevant VPJD data release."
title: "Vascular Plants of Japan Database (VPJD): Reproducible Research Workflows"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Jones"
    given-names: "Ben M."
    affiliation: "University of Oxford Botanic Garden and Arboretum; University of Oxford Department of Biology"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible R workflows supporting the Vascular Plants of Japan Database
  (VPJD), developed within the Oxford-Japan Plant Conservation Partnership
  (OJPCP). The repository provides version-controlled computational workflows
  for taxonomic reconciliation, data integration, geographic evidence
  processing, validation, and conservation analyses of the vascular flora
  of Japan.

repository-code: "https://github.com/alifeinthetrees/OJPCP-VPJD"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - "Vascular Plants of Japan Database"
  - "VPJD"
  - "Oxford-Japan Plant Conservation Partnership"
  - "OJPCP"
  - "vascular plants"
  - "Japan"
  - "plant conservation"
  - "taxonomy"
  - "biogeography"
  - "biodiversity informatics"
  - "conservation biology"
  - "reproducible research"
  - "R"
